IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mca-capacity-care`

-- Mental Capacity Act 2008, ss 3 to 8, 26, 28 and 42 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_mca.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a capable person making a risky choice` MEANS Assessment WITH
    `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain` IS FALSE
    `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation` IS TRUE
    `retains it, even briefly` IS TRUE
    `uses or weighs it` IS TRUE
    `communicates a decision by any means` IS TRUE
    `all practicable steps to help were taken` IS TRUE
    `the decision is unwise` IS TRUE

`a person with dementia who cannot weigh the options` MEANS Assessment WITH
    `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain` IS TRUE
    `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation` IS TRUE
    `retains it, even briefly` IS TRUE
    `uses or weighs it` IS FALSE
    `communicates a decision by any means` IS TRUE
    `all practicable steps to help were taken` IS TRUE
    `the decision is unwise` IS FALSE

`a person with dementia who understands with pictures` MEANS Assessment WITH
    `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain` IS TRUE
    `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation` IS TRUE
    `retains it, even briefly` IS TRUE
    `uses or weighs it` IS TRUE
    `communicates a decision by any means` IS TRUE
    `all practicable steps to help were taken` IS TRUE
    `the decision is unwise` IS FALSE

`a person who retains only briefly but decides` MEANS Assessment WITH
    `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain` IS TRUE
    `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation` IS TRUE
    `retains it, even briefly` IS TRUE
    `uses or weighs it` IS TRUE
    `communicates a decision by any means` IS TRUE
    `all practicable steps to help were taken` IS TRUE
    `the decision is unwise` IS FALSE

`a person unable to communicate, no help tried` MEANS Assessment WITH
