    `the decision is unwise` IS FALSE

`a confused person with no impairment of mind` MEANS Assessment WITH
    `has an impairment or disturbance of mind or brain` IS FALSE
    `understands the relevant information, with appropriate explanation` IS TRUE
    `retains it, even briefly` IS TRUE
    `uses or weighs it` IS FALSE
    `communicates a decision by any means` IS TRUE
    `all practicable steps to help were taken` IS TRUE
    `the decision is unwise` IS FALSE

`a careful care decision` MEANS BestInterests WITH
    `considered whether capacity may return` IS TRUE
    `encouraged participation` IS TRUE
    `considered past and present wishes, beliefs and values` IS TRUE
    `consulted carers, donees and deputies where practicable` IS TRUE
    `decided merely on age, appearance or condition` IS FALSE
    `motivated by a desire to bring about death` IS FALSE
    `is a property decision` IS FALSE
    `aimed to preserve the property for the person's own maintenance` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believes it is in the person's best interests` IS TRUE

`a decision made on age alone` MEANS BestInterests WITH
    `considered whether capacity may return` IS TRUE
    `encouraged participation` IS TRUE
    `considered past and present wishes, beliefs and values` IS TRUE
    `consulted carers, donees and deputies where practicable` IS TRUE
    `decided merely on age, appearance or condition` IS TRUE
    `motivated by a desire to bring about death` IS FALSE
    `is a property decision` IS FALSE
    `aimed to preserve the property for the person's own maintenance` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believes it is in the person's best interests` IS TRUE

