`a carer washing a confused parent` MEANS CareAct WITH
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS TRUE
    `is a restraint` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS FALSE
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS FALSE
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS FALSE
    `done negligently` IS FALSE

`a carer locking the door to stop wandering into traffic` MEANS CareAct WITH
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS TRUE
    `is a restraint` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS TRUE
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS TRUE
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS FALSE
    `done negligently` IS FALSE

`a carer locking the parent in all day for convenience` MEANS CareAct WITH
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS TRUE
    `is a restraint` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS FALSE
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS FALSE
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS FALSE
    `done negligently` IS FALSE

`a carer overriding the donee's decision` MEANS CareAct WITH
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS TRUE
    `is a restraint` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS FALSE
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS FALSE
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS TRUE
    `done negligently` IS FALSE

`a carer who never checked capacity` MEANS CareAct WITH
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS TRUE
    `is a restraint` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS FALSE
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS FALSE
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS FALSE
    `done negligently` IS FALSE

`a nurse who bathes negligently and scalds` MEANS CareAct WITH
    `took reasonable steps to establish capacity beforehand` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed P lacked capacity` IS TRUE
    `reasonably believed it was in P's best interests` IS TRUE
    `is a restraint` IS FALSE
    `reasonably believed it necessary to prevent harm to P` IS FALSE
    `proportionate to the likelihood and seriousness of harm` IS FALSE
    `contrary to a valid decision of a donee or deputy` IS FALSE
    `done negligently` IS TRUE

`a carer who starves a 70-year-old` MEANS IllTreatment WITH
    `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy` IS TRUE
    `P's age` IS 70
    `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably` IS TRUE
    `P died` IS FALSE

`a carer whose neglect kills an 80-year-old` MEANS IllTreatment WITH
    `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy` IS TRUE
    `P's age` IS 80
    `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably` IS TRUE
    `P died` IS TRUE

`a carer who neglects a 17-year-old` MEANS IllTreatment WITH
    `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy` IS TRUE
    `P's age` IS 17
    `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably` IS TRUE
    `P died` IS FALSE

`a carer who neglects a 15-year-old` MEANS IllTreatment WITH
    `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy` IS TRUE
    `P's age` IS 15
    `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably` IS TRUE
    `P died` IS FALSE

`a stranger who neglects nobody in their care` MEANS IllTreatment WITH
    `D cares for P, or is P's donee or deputy` IS FALSE
    `P's age` IS 70
    `abused, endangered or neglected P wilfully or unreasonably` IS TRUE
    `P died` IS FALSE

§ `ss 3 to 5`

#ASSERT NOT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a capable person making a risky choice`
#ASSERT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a person with dementia who cannot weigh the options`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a person with dementia who understands with pictures`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a person who retains only briefly but decides`
#ASSERT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a person unable to communicate, no help tried`
#ASSERT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a person unable to communicate after every effort`
#ASSERT `the person is unable to make the decision` `a confused person with no impairment of mind`

#ASSERT NOT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a capable person making a risky choice`
#ASSERT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a person with dementia who cannot weigh the options`
#ASSERT NOT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a person with dementia who understands with pictures`
#ASSERT NOT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a person who retains only briefly but decides`
#ASSERT NOT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a person unable to communicate, no help tried`
#ASSERT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a person unable to communicate after every effort`
#ASSERT NOT `the person lacks capacity for the decision` `a confused person with no impairment of mind`

#ASSERT NOT `the unwise decision alone shows incapacity` `a capable person making a risky choice`

#ASSERT `the Act's powers may be exercised for the person` 21
#ASSERT NOT `the Act's powers may be exercised for the person` 20
#ASSERT `the Act's powers may be exercised for the person` 85

§ `s 6`

#ASSERT `the decision complies with section 6` `a careful care decision`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision complies with section 6` `a decision made on age alone`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision complies with section 6` `a treatment decision aimed at ending life`
#ASSERT `the decision complies with section 6` `a sale of the home to pay for care`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision complies with section 6` `a sale of the home to fund a child's flat`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision complies with section 6` `a decision with no consultation`

§ `ss 7, 8`

#ASSERT `the act is protected by section 7` `a carer washing a confused parent`
#ASSERT `the act is protected by section 7` `a carer locking the door to stop wandering into traffic`
#ASSERT NOT `the act is protected by section 7` `a carer locking the parent in all day for convenience`
#ASSERT NOT `the act is protected by section 7` `a carer overriding the donee's decision`
#ASSERT NOT `the act is protected by section 7` `a carer who never checked capacity`
#ASSERT `the act is protected by section 7` `a nurse who bathes negligently and scalds`

#ASSERT NOT `the actor may still be liable in negligence` `a carer washing a confused parent`
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may still be liable in negligence` `a carer locking the door to stop wandering into traffic`
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may still be liable in negligence` `a carer locking the parent in all day for convenience`
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may still be liable in negligence` `a carer overriding the donee's decision`
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may still be liable in negligence` `a carer who never checked capacity`
#ASSERT `the actor may still be liable in negligence` `a nurse who bathes negligently and scalds`

§ `ss 26, 28`

#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `marriage`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `sexual touching`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `divorce on 3 years' separation`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `adoption`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `religion`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `gender reassignment`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `sterilisation`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `termination of pregnancy`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `an organ-transplant objection`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `an advance medical directive`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `a gift of the body`
#ASSERT NOT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `voting`
#ASSERT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `selling the home`
#ASSERT `the decision may be made on the person's behalf` `choosing a care home`

§ `s 42`

#ASSERT `D commits the ill-treatment offence` `a carer who starves a 70-year-old`
#ASSERT `D commits the ill-treatment offence` `a carer whose neglect kills an 80-year-old`
#ASSERT `D commits the ill-treatment offence` `a carer who neglects a 17-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `D commits the ill-treatment offence` `a carer who neglects a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `D commits the ill-treatment offence` `a stranger who neglects nobody in their care`

#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for ill-treatment` `a carer who starves a 70-year-old` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for ill-treatment` `a carer whose neglect kills an 80-year-old` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for ill-treatment` `a carer who neglects a 17-year-old` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for ill-treatment` `a carer who neglects a 15-year-old` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for ill-treatment` `a stranger who neglects nobody in their care` EQUALS 8

